 'In a right triangle, the side adjacent to angle θ is 20 and the hypotenuse is 29. What is cos θ?', 0,
 '[{"text": "20/29", "feedback": "Correct. cos θ = adjacent ÷ hypotenuse = 20/29."}, {"text": "29/20", "feedback": "This ratio is upside down — cosine is adjacent over hypotenuse, not the other way around."}, {"text": "21/29", "feedback": "21 isn''t one of the two given values — cosine only needs the adjacent side and the hypotenuse, both already given."}, {"text": "9/29", "feedback": "9 isn''t one of the two given values — cosine only needs the adjacent side and the hypotenuse, both already given."}]'::jsonb,
 'trig-ratio-basic'),
('MPM2D', 'trigonometry', 'the-primary-trig-ratios', 6, 'Easy',
 'In a right triangle, the hypotenuse is which side?', 3,
