('MPM2D', 'trigonometry', 'the-primary-trig-ratios', 11, 'Medium',
 'In a right triangle, the side opposite angle θ is 9 and the adjacent side is 12. What is tan θ, as a fraction in lowest terms?', 1,
 '[{"text": "4/3", "feedback": "This ratio is upside down — tangent is opposite over adjacent, not the other way around."}, {"text": "3/4", "feedback": "Correct. tan θ = opposite ÷ adjacent = 9/12, which simplifies to 3/4."}, {"text": "9/12", "feedback": "This is correct before simplifying — reduce the fraction 9/12 to lowest terms."}, {"text": "9/15", "feedback": "15 isn''t the adjacent side — tangent uses only the opposite and adjacent sides, not the hypotenuse."}]'::jsonb,
 'trig-ratio-tangent-simplify'),
('MPM2D', 'trigonometry', 'the-primary-trig-ratios', 12, 'Medium',
 'In a right triangle, sin θ = 7/25. What is cos θ?', 3,
 '[{"text": "18/25", "feedback": "This subtracts 7 from 25 directly instead of using the Pythagorean theorem to find the missing side."}, {"text": "7/25", "feedback": "This reuses sine''s value for cosine — cosine compares a different pair of sides than sine does."}, {"text": "25/24", "feedback": "This has the ratio upside down, and 25 isn''t the adjacent side — cosine is adjacent over hypotenuse, and the hypotenuse here is 25."}, {"text": "24/25", "feedback": "Correct. With opposite = 7 and hypotenuse = 25, the adjacent side is √(25²−7²) = √576 = 24 (a 7-24-25 triangle), so cos θ = adjacent ÷ hypotenuse = 24/25."}]'::jsonb,
 'trig-ratio-from-another-ratio'),
('MPM2D', 'trigonometry', 'the-primary-trig-ratios', 13, 'Medium',
 'In a right triangle, the hypotenuse is 26 and the side adjacent to θ is 10. What is sin θ, as a fraction in lowest terms?', 2,
 '[{"text": "10/26", "feedback": "This uses the adjacent side, not the opposite side — sine needs the side opposite θ, which still needs to be found using the Pythagorean theorem."}, {"text": "5/13", "feedback": "This simplifies 10/26 instead of first finding the actual opposite side using the Pythagorean theorem."}, {"text": "12/13", "feedback": "Correct. With adjacent = 10 and hypotenuse = 26, the opposite side is √(26²−10²) = √576 = 24 (a 10-24-26 triangle), so sin θ = 24÷26 = 12/13 in lowest terms."}, {"text": "24/26", "feedback": "This is correct before simplifying — reduce the fraction 24/26 to lowest terms."}]'::jsonb,
 'trig-ratio-find-missing-side-first'),
('MPM2D', 'trigonometry', 'the-primary-trig-ratios', 14, 'Medium',
 'In a right triangle, tan θ = 8/15. What is sin θ?', 0,
 '[{"text": "8/17", "feedback": "Correct. tan θ = opposite÷adjacent = 8/15, so the hypotenuse is √(8²+15²) = √289 = 17 (an 8-15-17 triangle), and sin θ = opposite÷hypotenuse = 8/17."}, {"text": "15/17", "feedback": "This is cos θ, not sin θ — sine uses the side opposite θ (8), not the adjacent side (15)."}, {"text": "8/15", "feedback": "This reuses tan θ''s value directly — sine needs the hypotenuse in its ratio, which tan θ doesn''t include."}, {"text": "15/8", "feedback": "This ratio is upside down and uses the wrong pair of sides — sine is opposite over hypotenuse, not adjacent over opposite."}]'::jsonb,
 'trig-ratio-from-tangent'),
