 'In a right triangle, sin θ = 9/41. What is cos θ?', 3,
 '[{"text": "9/41", "feedback": "This reuses sine''s value for cosine — cosine compares a different pair of sides than sine does."}, {"text": "32/41", "feedback": "Recompute the adjacent side using the Pythagorean theorem: √(41²−9²) — this doesn''t come out to 32."}, {"text": "41/40", "feedback": "This has the ratio upside down, and 41 isn''t the adjacent side — cosine is adjacent over hypotenuse, and the hypotenuse here is 41."}, {"text": "40/41", "feedback": "Correct. With opposite = 9 and hypotenuse = 41, the adjacent side is √(41²−9²) = √1600 = 40 (a 9-40-41 triangle), so cos θ = 40÷41."}]'::jsonb,
 'trig-ratio-from-another-ratio'),
