 'In a right triangle, cos θ = 11/61. What is tan θ?', 0,
 '[{"text": "60/11", "feedback": "Correct. With adjacent = 11 and hypotenuse = 61, the opposite side is √(61²−11²) = √3600 = 60 (an 11-60-61 triangle), so tan θ = opposite÷adjacent = 60/11."}, {"text": "11/60", "feedback": "This ratio is upside down — tangent is opposite over adjacent; recheck which side goes on top."}, {"text": "61/60", "feedback": "This uses the hypotenuse instead of the adjacent side — tangent is opposite over adjacent, with no hypotenuse involved."}, {"text": "11/61", "feedback": "This reuses cos θ''s value directly — tangent needs a different pair of sides than cosine."}]'::jsonb,
