('MPM2D', 'trigonometry', 'trig-for-side-lengths', 39, 'Advanced',
 'A 1.8 m tall observer stands 40 m from a tower and measures the angle of elevation to its top as 22°. Find the height of the tower, to one decimal place.', 0,
 '[{"text": "18.0 m", "feedback": "Correct. The height above eye level is 40 × tan(22°) ≈ 16.2 m; adding the observer''s own height of 1.8 m gives a total tower height of about 18.0 m."}, {"text": "16.2 m", "feedback": "This is 40 × tan(22°) alone — remember to add the observer''s own eye height, since the angle is measured from their eyes, not the ground."}, {"text": "21.8 m", "feedback": "This adds 1.8 to a slightly incorrect value — recompute 40 × tan(22°) more precisely first."}, {"text": "41.8 m", "feedback": "This just adds the observer''s height to the horizontal distance — the vertical rise above eye level (40×tan(22°)) is what needs to be added instead."}]'::jsonb,
 'elevation-with-observer-height'),
('MPM2D', 'trigonometry', 'trig-for-side-lengths', 40, 'Advanced',
