('MPM2D', 'trigonometry', 'trig-for-angles', 7, 'Challenge',
 'A right triangle has a hypotenuse of 25 and an adjacent side of 7. Find both acute angles, to the nearest degree.', 0,
 '[{"text": "74° and 16°", "feedback": "Correct. cos⁻¹(7÷25) ≈ 74°, and since the two acute angles are complementary, the other is 90°−74° = 16°."}, {"text": "16° and 74°, but using sin⁻¹(7÷25) for the first", "feedback": "sin⁻¹(7÷25) doesn''t give 16° — the side 7 is adjacent to the angle being found, so cosine (not sine) is the correct ratio to start with."}, {"text": "54° and 36°", "feedback": "Recheck cos⁻¹(7÷25) directly — these values don''t match that calculation."}, {"text": "73° and 17°", "feedback": "Close, but recompute cos⁻¹(7÷25) more precisely, then subtract from 90° for the second angle."}]'::jsonb,
