 'A right triangle''s two acute angles are in the ratio 1:2. Find both acute angles.', 3,
 '[{"text": "45° and 45°", "feedback": "A 1:1 ratio would give two equal angles — but the ratio given here is 1:2, not 1:1."}, {"text": "20° and 70°", "feedback": "Check this ratio: 20:70 simplifies to 2:7, not 1:2 — set up x and 2x, then solve x+2x=90."}, {"text": "40° and 50°", "feedback": "Check this ratio: 40:50 simplifies to 4:5, not 1:2 — set up x and 2x, then solve x+2x=90."}, {"text": "30° and 60°", "feedback": "Correct. Let the angles be x and 2x; since they''re complementary, x+2x=90 gives 3x=90, so x=30, and the angles are 30° and 60°."}]'::jsonb,
